    [BugFix][Worker] Skip Eagle3 PP aux patch for MiniMax-M3 (#18371)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    MiniMax-M3 already propagates Eagle3 auxiliary hidden states across
    pipeline stages. The generic Eagle3 PP patch overwrites its native
    implementation.
    
    Return `False` specifically for `MiniMaxM3Model`, preserving its native
    `forward` and intermediate-tensor methods. Other Eagle models retain the
    existing patch behavior, regardless of
    `supports_aux_hidden_states_over_pp`.
    
    Add the English TODO: `Remove this patch after MiniMax-M2.7 is sunset.`
    
    Main-branch counterpart of #18370. Both changed files are byte-for-byte
    identical to the release PR.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No API change. MiniMax-M3 keeps its native Eagle3 PP implementation;
    other models continue to receive the patch.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - On this main branch: Ruff check/format and `git diff --check` passed;
    verified both changed files exactly match #18370.
    - The identical change in #18370 passed all **10 tests** in
    `tests/ut/patch/worker/test_patch_eagle3_pp_aux.py`, covering native M3
    methods and continued patching of other Eagle models.
    - Existing NPU validation was performed on **releases/v0.30.0 plus this
    change**, using MRV2, PP2 / DP2 / TP4, EP8 per stage, flashcomm1,
    Eagle3, and `FULL_DECODE_ONLY`. One curl request returned **HTTP 200**,
    with **4547 input tokens and 3072 output tokens**, and coherent output.
    - The main branch has not been separately rerun on NPU; main integration
    is left to CI. Full `format.sh ci` on the earlier validation environment
    was blocked by its Node 12 version (markdownlint requires Node >=20).
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607
    
    Signed-off-by: CXY-Katrina <katrina.cxy@gmail.com>

